  "body": "The maintainer reported this in chat (2026-11-15): \"Bug; Application icon is not showing up in status bar on windows\".\n\nWhat happens: On Windows, the taskbar shows no CamCraft icon for the running application. We read \"status bar\" as the Windows taskbar. The reporter did not say if the window title bar and Alt+Tab show the icon.\n\nExpected: The taskbar button, the window title bar and Alt+Tab show the CamCraft icon (the icon of issue 1459).\n\nWhere to look:\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/app_icon.rs` sets the window icon at run time.\n- The Windows executable possibly has no embedded icon resource. Windows uses the embedded resource for the taskbar button and for the file in Explorer.\n\nConstraints:\n- A change to a `build.rs` or a new build dependency needs the maintainer's decision. State it in the PR body.\n- The build must stay unchanged on Linux and macOS.\n\nDone means:\n- The Windows build shows the CamCraft icon in the taskbar, the title bar and Alt+Tab.\n- A test pins that the icon data loads and has a correct size. The PR body says that a hand check on Windows is owed, because agents do not start the GUI.\n",
